{%- comment -%}
  Screens: magic-link login, link sent.
  Both are mock frontend states — no credential is exchanged here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- 1. Magic-link login ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen spp__centred" data-spp-screen="login" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-login-h">
  <div style="padding:26px 4px;">
    <div class="spp__disc spp__disc--sm" style="background:#EAF6FD;color:#47B5E9;">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'paw', size: 30 %}
    </div>

    <h1 class="spp__h1 spp__h1--lg" id="spp-login-h" style="font-size:27px;line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:10px;">Manage your VetPets routine</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede" style="max-width:340px;margin:0 auto 26px;font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;">
      Enter the email you used at checkout. We&rsquo;ll send a sign-in link &mdash; no password to remember.
    </p>

    <form class="spp__card" style="text-align:left;border-radius:18px;" data-spp-form="login" novalidate>
      <label class="spp__field-label" for="spp-email">Email address</label>
      {%- comment -%}
        NO `value` ATTRIBUTE. The field starts genuinely empty in every mode.

        It once shipped with a prototype address prefilled, which reached real
        customers: they had to select and delete a stranger's email before
        typing their own. A placeholder is the only thing that belongs here —
        it is not a value, so it disappears the moment the customer types.

        The attributes below are what make this pleasant on a phone: no
        auto-capitalised first letter, no spellcheck underline, the email
        keyboard, and the browser's own saved-address autofill.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input
        class="spp__input spp__input--lg"
        id="spp-email"
        name="email"
        type="email"
        inputmode="email"
        autocomplete="email"
        autocapitalize="none"
        autocorrect="off"
        spellcheck="false"
        placeholder="you@example.com"
        required
      >
      <p class="spp__note" data-spp-error="login" role="alert" hidden style="color:#D92D20;margin-top:8px;"></p>

      <button type="submit" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:14px;" data-spp-act="sendLink">
        <span data-spp-field="label.sendLink">Email me a sign-in link</span>
        {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'arrow-right', stroke: '#fff' %}
      </button>

      <p class="spp__note" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;">
        The link stays valid for 15 minutes and opens straight into your subscriptions.
      </p>
    </form>

    <p style="margin:22px 0 0;font:500 14px/1.5 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-body);">
      Bought as a guest? <a href="#" data-spp-go="account">Contact support</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 2. Link sent ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen spp__centred" data-spp-screen="sent" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-sent-h">
  <div style="padding:34px 4px;">
    <div class="spp__disc spp__disc--light" style="width:74px;height:74px;margin-bottom:22px;">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'check', size: 34, stroke: '#47B5E9' %}
    </div>

    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-sent-h" style="font-size:26px;margin-bottom:10px;">Check your inbox</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede" style="max-width:330px;margin:0 auto 8px;font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;">
      We sent a sign-in link to <strong style="color:var(--spp-ink);" data-spp-field="customer.email">your email address</strong>.
      Open it on this device to land straight in your account.
    </p>

    <div class="spp__card" style="margin:24px 0 18px;text-align:left;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:none;">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;">
        <span style="flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:2px;color:var(--spp-accent);">
          {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'clock', size: 20 %}
        </span>
        <p style="margin:0;font:500 14.5px/1.5 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-body);">
          Links expire after 15 minutes. Requesting a new one cancels the previous link.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Both of these are prototype affordances and are removed in live mode.

      "Open the link (demo)" short-circuits the magic link, which is the whole
      security boundary. "Resend link" replays the address the mock adapter
      remembers; live mode deliberately never holds the customer's email in the
      browser, so it would post an empty one. The live path to both is the same
      and it is already on this screen: open the emailed link, or use "Use a
      different email" to start again.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" data-spp-mock-only data-spp-act="openLink">Open the link (demo)</button>
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--secondary" style="margin-top:10px;" data-spp-mock-only data-spp-act="resend">
      <span data-spp-field="label.resend">Resend link</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" style="margin-top:6px;" data-spp-go="login">Use a different email</button>
  </div>
</section>
